    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a1">

                <pb facs="0092" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg32"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 131.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morton to Mr.
                            Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Agriculture</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    your consideration a letter which has just been received from Patterson, Ramsay
                    &amp; Co., steamship agents, Baltimore, Md., in regard to the Belgian
                    prohibition of American cattle. If it appears possible to accomplish anything in
                    the way of securing the removal of this prohibition I would recommend that the
                    matter be given the early attention of your Department.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Sterling
                    Morton</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
